@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ v2.0 covers two things: hydrogens (a proper Show hydrogens option and complete h
 ## Project
 - New `src/core/hydrogens.mjs`; `src/core/layout2d.mjs` gained explicit-H placement, label text and charge helpers; `src/core/session.mjs` has the new `elements` setting and the hydrogens-off default.
 - `node tools/build_viewer.mjs` writes `js/generated/hydrogens.js`, `layout2d.js` and `labs.js` from `src/` (see the next section). Run it after editing `hydrogens.mjs`, `layout2d.mjs` or `src/labs`.
-- **Tests:** 159 Node tests pass (58 new). The browser suite has 54 of 59 passing, with new or rewritten cases 44, 50-59 and updates to 02, 04, 36, 39, 41, 43. The browser tests open the details panel first (it starts closed); test 57 covers the closed default.
+- **Tests:** 217 Node tests pass. The browser suite has 57 of 62 passing, with new or rewritten cases 44, 50-62 and updates to 02, 04, 36, 39, 41, 43. The browser tests open the details panel first (it starts closed); test 57 covers the closed default.
 
 ## 5. Project structure: the single HTML file is split
 `laura-viewer.html` (300 KB with inline CSS and three inline scripts) is now `index.html` (52 KB, markup only) plus `css/` (9 files) and `js/` (31 files). The layout, load order and rules are in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
@@ -44,9 +44,19 @@ v2.0 covers two things: hydrogens (a proper Show hydrogens option and complete h
 - **Three deliberate code changes**, all about start-up: the render loop and the "restore saved imports" call now start from `js/main.js` instead of during load (`renderLoop`, `restoreSavedImports`), and `esc()` moved into `constants.js`. This is a precaution (with many script files a frame or callback could in principle fire between two of them); I could not make the old order fail in testing.
 - `tools/build_viewer.mjs` now writes the generated files (it no longer edits the HTML); `--check` verifies they are current. New tests: `tests/structure.test.mjs`, `tests/generated.test.mjs`.
 
+## 6. Lone electron pairs
+- **Show lone pairs** (Display Options, **off by default**; saved in sessions) draws each lone pair in Ball and stick view as a translucent purple lobe with two white electron dots, so it cannot be mistaken for an atom (solid CPK colours) or a bond (grey cylinders). **They are not atoms:** they are not in the structure, are not pickable, selectable or measurable, and do not change any atom count. The details panel states "Lone pairs (not atoms): N".
+- **How many (from valence):** lone pairs = (valence electrons - charge - bond-order sum) / 2, for N, O, S, P, Se and the halogens. Water O 2, ammonia N 1, amine N 1, alcohol/ether O 2, carbonyl O 2, thiol/H2S S 2, halide 3, N2 / HCN N / CO 1 each (CO's carbon too). Charges are read off the structure the same way the 2D diagram does (NH3+ has none; carboxylate O- has 3).
+- **Where (from the real geometry, i.e. electron-region geometry):** tetrahedral for sp3 atoms (water, alcohols, ethers, amines, ammonia: the lobes point away from the substituents); in the molecular plane at 120 degrees for a carbonyl O or a pyridine N; perpendicular to the plane for a lone pair conjugated with a pi system (aniline or amide N, phenol O: a "p" lone pair, drawn on one face); straight away from the bond for linear atoms.
+- **Never guessed:** an atom that looks short of bonds (usually because hydrogens are missing from the file) gets no lone pair, so a missing N-H cannot appear as a lone pair; without any hydrogens, delocalised ring atoms are skipped too (a ring N could be pyridine-type or N-H). A lone pair that is part of an aromatic pi system (imidazole's N-H, pyrrole, furan's second pair) is not shown.
+- **Verified:** `tests/lonepairs.test.mjs` (46 tests) checks every built-in molecule against its Lewis structure written out by hand (31 small molecules; peptide models 3n+2 per chain; B-DNA is schematic) and the geometry with real angles (water LP-O-H and LP-O-LP ~109 degrees and opposite the hydrogens; ammonia opposite the three N-H; formaldehyde in plane at 120 degrees; aniline perpendicular to the ring; ...). Four deliberately injected bugs are each caught. Browser tests 60-62 cover the toggle, the counts in the scene, "not atoms", independence from the hydrogen switch, the notices and session round trip.
+- **Needed one fix elsewhere:** the shared "as drawn" helper (`drawnOrdersAndCharges` in `layout2d.mjs`) now shows a delocalised group that carries an O-H as a protonated acid (C=O and C-OH). The peptide models' C-terminus (COOH) had been read as a carboxylate; the 2D diagram benefits as well.
+- New files: `src/core/lonepairs.mjs` (-> `js/generated/lonepairs.js`) and `js/viewer/lone-pairs.js` (drawing).
+
 ## Limits
 - **3D rendering could not be exercised here:** the browser suite runs on a Three.js stand-in, so the label *logic* (which symbols, where, how big, overlap, zoom) is tested and its alignment was checked against an independent perspective calculation, but it has not been seen on the real renderer. Please look at it once in a browser; the thresholds (`EL_ON_PX`, `EL_OFF_PX`, `EL_SHOW`, `EL_HIDE`, `EL_CAP`, `EL_MAX_ATOMS` near `elementLabels` in the viewer) are one-line changes. The flicker fix was measured, not seen: I could not reproduce your exact glitch on the real renderer, so if labels still misbehave, tell me what you see (flicker, wrong position, overlap, wrong size).
 - Peptide models are larger now (Ala₁₂ has 123 atoms, not 60): with hydrogens hidden you see 61 atoms. The Mirror and Bond-rotation labs limit molecules to 80 atoms and use the whole molecule (hydrogens included), so they decline the longer peptides; the 3D labs do not follow the Hydrogens switch.
 - Hidden hydrogens in 2D are only counted from hydrogen atoms that exist in the data; the app does not invent hydrogens for heavy-atom-only imports.
 - A symbol sits on the sphere centre, so it can be partly covered where another atom's sphere overlaps its edge; that is a normal consequence of overlapping spheres. A label that has just become hidden or overlapped can linger for up to about 0.2 s (it fades), by design.
 - **Browser suite:** 5 cases fail exactly as they did in v1.9 (11, 20: they look for a "Teaching, session" section that v1.9 renamed; 39; 46: expects the white outline v1.9 removed; 47). Because test 11 is stale, the session round trip was checked by hand instead (hydrogens and element-label choices survive save and reload; sessions without the new fields load with hydrogens hidden and labels on). `tests/blender_mock_check.py` hits the same stale section name. None of these relate to this work.
+- **Lone pairs:** the 3D lobes (size, colour, translucency) were checked against an independent projection of the page's data, not on the real renderer; the constants are at the top of `js/viewer/lone-pairs.js` and `drawLonePairs`. Lone pairs are not drawn in the 2D diagram or in Chains view, and not for structures over 6,000 atoms. A conjugated (p) lone pair is drawn as one lobe on one face of the plane, not as a two-lobed p orbital.
